<title>POLAND: BPH to issue $100 mln bond on May 22.</title>
<headline>BPH to issue $100 mln bond on May 22.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Przemyslowo-Handlowy SA (BPH) will issue its convertible bond in London on May 22, the bank said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;On May 15, 1997, the International Information Memorandum and agreements connected to the issue of bonds convertible into shares of BPH have been signed in London,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;The transaction will be carried out on May 22,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>It did not give any further details but earlier the bank's shareholders approved a $100 million five-year bond exchangeable for up to 1,994,000 shares issued ex-rights. Bank officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
